EXO-201: the XL330 is an exclusion volume and the module CARRIES it - the proxy body EXO-187 built beside every module is gone (it only duplicated the real one and z-fought with it in the viewport). The real actuator bodies below take part in the interference check; measured, `XL330 v2/Body1` is x -10.0..10.0, y -9.5..24.5 from its back z -36.5 on up (past the stator underside -24.5, where it is inside the stator's own solid) - the proxy rectangle to 0.000 mm. Each landing plate's opening is that footprint grown by ACT_OPEN_MARGIN 0.0 (EXO-193: the hand-made opening, validated with the real actuator), cut through the whole volume (z -36.5..-24.5); every BODY of every link was checked against the volume grown by MIN_CLEARANCE 1.0 in pure Python before the build and would have been refused by name; the EXO-183 collar is a blend tangent to the plate, so its bar is the XL330's own box (EXO-193).
